      ":question/worked-solution": "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x^{3} \\tan{\\left(y \\right)}-3^{x + y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x^{3} \\tan{\\left(y \\right)})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3^{x}\\cdot 3^{y}) \\\\  & =x^{3}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\tan{\\left(y \\right)})-3^{x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3^{y}) \\\\  & =x^{3}\\cdot \\sec^{2}{\\left(y \\right)}-3^{x}\\cdot 3^{y} \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} \\\\  & =- 3^{x + y} \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} + x^{3} \\sec^{2}{\\left(y \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
